  "path": "/api/jobs/{id}/send",
  "summary": "Send a held job's request (PLAN-4 D16) - as it was built, or changed for this one request. With no body, or an empty one, it is sent exactly as built. `request` replaces the request whole; `gen` sets parameters over the ones it was built with - any parameter a job may name, never the queue's own three (`model`, `n`, `retries`), which its record names as it was submitted - and `unset` names parameters to leave unnamed, so that the model's settings, then the bootstrap's, apply again. The request and its parameters are held to the rules a submit's are, and refused the same way (`bad_request`, `bad_max_tokens`, `out_of_range`, and `bad_audio_request` for a whisper model's request that is not one), never sent. The job is queued again in its place, and its turn runs what was sent - never built again - counted by its model before the model is asked, as every job's turn is. The request record keeps both: `request.json` and `held.json`, what was built, and `sent.json`, what was sent - `tuned` when it differs from what was built, naming each thing `changed`. The job says so for as long as it is kept: `check` is `tuned` for a request changed before it was sent, `sent` for one sent as built - a tuned request is never mistaken for a normal one. A job that is not held is refused `not_held`, with its status.",
